    "message": "Test that installed toilets reach the frame and the demo-v2 map\n\nThe floor-plan placement fix was covered only down to the overlay\ngeometry, so nothing checked that the browser receives and draws the\nnew toilets. The new tests build frames through the timeline route,\nboth from the frame cache at a saved boundary and reconstructed at\nanother minute, and check that each installed toilet has a map point\ninside its zone. They then run demo-v2-scene.js, demo-v2-sprites.js\nand demo-v2-map.js in node with a canvas stand-in and check the\nfacility hits HinanjoMap.draw returns: every toilet is drawn at its\nown position on both the physical map and the schematic.\n\nOn the code before the placement fix, the frame and physical-map\ntests fail while the schematic test passes: the schematic lays\nfacilities out by zone and showed the new toilets even though they\nhad no floor-plan point. A further test pins that the physical map\nomits a facility without a point.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
